  "scope": "A disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 cluster with bundled kindnet compares the same protected client's HTTP model downloads before and after a native NetworkPolicy. The policy allows CoreDNS and the exact labeled proxy namespace and Pods. The case checks in-cluster Service and direct Pod IP paths and a case-owned off-cluster Docker peer on an internal bridge. The unselected namespace can still reach denied targets. A supplemental application proxy maps one exact source identifier to fixed bytes from an owned in-cluster upstream and refuses a different owned source before fetching it. These application source rules are separate from NetworkPolicy selectors. The synthetic JSON requests use TCP/8080. Production telemetry, public-hub and domain identity, provider paths and non-Pod consumers are open.",
